 75BR    75KR EC DECAY (4.60 M)        1995BEZS,1974HO35,1974RO1213NDS    201309
 75BR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=ALEXANDRU NEGRET, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 114, 841 (2013)$    
 75BR2 H CUT=30-Jun-2013$                                                       
 75BR DG CC$ FROM BrIcc v2.3 (9-Dec-2011) 2008Ki07, "Frozen Orbitals" appr.     
 75BR c  1995BeZS: Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, ce, half-life using HPGe detectors, 
 75BR2c  a mini-orange electron spectrometer for the determination of           
 75BR3c  internal conversion coefficients, and a positron annihilator.          
 75BR4c  {+75}Kr source prepared in {+58}Ni({+20}Ne,2pn) reaction at            
 75BR5c  4.2 MeV/nucleon beam energy from GSI Unilac accelerator followed       
 75BR6c  by mass separation                                                     
 75BR c  1974Ho35 (also 1973HoYM thesis): Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, ce. A total  
 75BR2c  of 32 |g rays reported placed amongst 15 excited states. {+75}Kr       
 75BR3c  produced in {+79}Br(p,5n) E=65 MeV reaction; Kr gas separated from     
 75BR4c  other elements by cold traps. No information was deduced from ce data  
 75BR c  1974Ro12 (also 1974Ro11): Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, ce, E|b {+75}Kr     
 75BR2c  formed in Zr(p,5pxn) E=600 MeV reaction at CERN-ISOLDE facility        
 75BR3c  followed by mass separation. A total of 16 |g rays reported with ce    
 75BR4c  data for three |g transitions. A 6.5-keV |g ray reported belongs to    
 75BR5c  the decay of {+75}Br to {+75}Se. Measured level lifetimes by |g|g(t)   
 75BR c  Others: 1975CoZR, 1973DaYM, 1969Ha03, 1960Gr19, 1960Bu22               
 75BR c  Measured annihilation radiation intensity: 250 {I50} (1975CoZR).       
 75BR2c  Other: 607 {I60} (1974Ho35)                                            
 75BR c  Most data given here are from 1995BeZS. The level scheme originally    
 75BR2c  proposed in 1974Ho35 and 1974Ro12 has been extended and greatly        
 75BR3c  modified based on their detailed |g|g coincidence measurements         
 75BR cG $Following |g rays reported by 1974Ho35 have not been seen in 1995BeZS:
 75BR2cG E|g=692.8 {I4}, I|g=0.07 {I6} placed from an 824.7 level;              
 75BR3cG E|g=698.2 {I4}, I|g=0.26 {I3} placed from 1072.5 level;                
 75BR4cG E|g=787.6 {I4}, I|g=0.39 {I4} placed from 1612.3 level;                
 75BR5cG E|g=1356.9 {I5}, I|g=0.39 {I6} placed from a 2958.7 level.             
 75BR6cG These |g rays have been omitted here                                   
 75BR cG E,RI$From 1995BeZS, unless otherwise stated. The I|g values in         
 75BR2cG 1995BeZS are normalized to 100 disintegrations of {+75}Kr. Energy      
 75BR3cG uncertainty of 0.3 keV is assigned for most transitions in consultation
 75BR4cG Dr. B. Rubio (adviser of 1995BeZS thesis) through e-mail reply         
 75BR5cG of April 5. Several lines are indicated by 1995BeZS as contaminated    
 75BR6cG with other activities. The evaluators assume that appropriate          
 75BR7cG corrections have been applied to the values listed in table 3.2 of     
 75BR8cG 1995BeZS                                                               
 75BR cG M,MR$From Adopted Gammas, based on measured |a(K)exp, |a(L)exp and     
 75BR2cG |a(M)exp values in 1995BeZS. Mixing ratios deduced by the evaluators   
 75BR3cG from ce data in 1995BeZS                                               
 75BR cG E(A)$ Contamination from a line in {+75}Rb decay                       
 75BR cG E(B)$ Contamination from a sum peak of either two transitions in       
 75BR2cG cascade or a gamma ray summing with 511-keV annihilation peak          
 75BR cG E(C)$ Contamination from room background                               
 75BR cG E(D)$ Contamination from a line from {+75}Br decay                     
 75BR cG E(H)$ Observed in |g|g coin spectrum, not in singles                   
 75BR cG E(I)$ Contaminated with 511-keV annihilation peak                      
 75BR cG E(K)$ Transition observed in an experiment at HMI by producing {+75}Kr 
 75BR2cG source in {+58}Ni({+20}Ne,2pn) at 80 MeV using OSIRIS detector system  
 75BR3cG for |g-ray detection (some details are given in appendix C of 1995BeZS)
 75BR cG RI(G)$ From |g|g coincidence gated spectrum                            
